Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim states that the Inglis Barracks bombing was the first IRA attack in England since a bombing whose purpose was to kill Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher. The evidence confirms that the last IRA attack in England before the Inglis Barracks bombing was the 1996 Docklands bombing. However, the purpose of the Inglis Barracks bombing is not established in the evidence, and no source directly confirms that the Brighton hotel bombing (1984) was the last attack with the stated purpose of killing Thatcher. Further evidence is needed to confirm the intent of the Inglis Barracks bombing and to verify the timeline of attacks with assassination intent.
